    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0592" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.151/144: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Aldridge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-27T12:00:00+02:00">July 27,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received July 27—8:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>105. My July 12 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>] 2 p.m. At the request of Mr.
                    Maximos, to whom I had fully explained the Ulen difficulties as soon as he
                    became Foreign Minister, I took Mr. Shepperd<anchor n="35" xml:id="d413-f1"/>
                    personally to the Foreign Office yesterday and the two men worked out a
                    compromise agreement. The agreement was a verbal one and was not worked out in
                    complete detail, as it was reached an hour before Mr. Shepperd left for the
                    United States. For the time being, however, it apparently settles the company’s
                    difficulties and Mr. Shepperd has expressed his satisfaction.<anchor n="36"
                        xml:id="d413-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Aldridge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d413-f1" n="35" xml:id="d413-f1-content">
                <p>Thomas S. Shepperd, of Ulen &amp; Co.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d413-f2" n="36" xml:id="d413-f2-content">
                <p>In despatch No. 797, August 28, 1935, the Chargé in Greece reported that written
                    agreements dated August 16, 1935, were concluded in accordance with the previous
                    verbal arrangement with Mr. Shepperd (868.151/150).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
